# KEYMAP.md, opening principles: "Over a terminal grid no bare key is ever an app
# affordance", and §Workspace (Terminal mode): "All keys go to the PTY except these direct
# terminal affordances" (`cmd-c`, `cmd-v`, `ctrl-s`). `ctrl-c` is named there too — it
# "remains the PTY interrupt" and is never a Fleet clipboard or quit binding.
#
# Every key pressed below is a Hub affordance: `j`/`k` move a cursor, `J` opens the jobs
# panel, `?` help, `:` the palette, `/` the filter, `!` the sticky error [A18], `i` the
# detail panel, `H` the rail [A22], `a`/`A` the agent popup [A21], `p` the PR screen, `1` a
# context, `y` copy, `N` a new context. Over a grid they are all just characters, and the
# proof is that they come back in `terminal.text` in the order they were typed.
fixture: one-repo
await idle
key o
await screen == Workspace 20000

# Our own shell tab; see terminal-text.scenario for why the `wait` is here and why it is
# the only one.
key ctrl-s c
await lists.tabs.rows[3] exists 20000
await lists.tabs.selected.id == 4 20000
wait 1500
await terminal.text ~= \S 20000
type PS1="fleet-$((6*7))-ready> "
key enter
await terminal.text ~= fleet-42-ready 20000
assert focused == tabs.tab[3]

# Sixteen app affordances, pressed bare. Nothing may open and nothing may move.
key j k J ? : / q ! i H a A p n 1 y N
await terminal.text ~= "jkJ\?:/q!iHaApn1yN" 20000
assert screen == Workspace && mode == Terminal && overlay absent
assert agents.popup absent && dialog absent && focused == tabs.tab[3]
shot terminal-owns-keys
dump terminal-owns-keys

# The prefix is the exception, and it is one-shot: `b` is bound to nothing in the table, so
# it is swallowed rather than forwarded. The `Z` that follows lands directly after the `N`,
# which is only true if no `b` reached the PTY.
key ctrl-s b
await mode == Terminal 10000
key Z
await terminal.text ~= "jkJ\?:/q!iHaApn1yNZ" 20000

# `ctrl-c` is the PTY's interrupt, not a Fleet key: the shell abandons the line it was
# given and prompts again, and Fleet is exactly where it was. The line is never submitted,
# so bash never tries to history-expand the `!` in it.
key ctrl-c
await terminal.text ~= "\^C\nfleet-42-ready>" 20000
assert screen == Workspace && mode == Terminal && overlay absent
quit
